  description: Americium is a radioactive transuranic chemical element with symbol
    Am and atomic number 95. This member of the actinide series is located in the
    periodic table under the lanthanide element europium, and thus by analogy was
    named after the Americas. Americium was first produced in 1944 by the group of
    Glenn T.Seaborg from Berkeley, California, at the metallurgical laboratory of
    University of Chicago.
